The more.

7
00:00:25.417 --> 00:00:27.532
The more means used for a growing amount.

8
00:00:28.117 --> 00:00:29.431
The more I read...

9
00:00:30.017 --> 00:00:32.750
Your turn. Say: The more.

10
00:00:35.600 --> 00:00:36.334
The more.

11
00:00:37.083 --> 00:00:38.061
The less.

12
00:00:39.050 --> 00:00:41.502
The less means used for a smaller amount.

13
00:00:42.117 --> 00:00:43.501
The less I worry...

14
00:00:44.117 --> 00:00:46.873
Your turn. Say: The less.

15
00:00:49.733 --> 00:00:50.839
The less.

16
00:00:51.583 --> 00:00:52.375
The better.

17
00:00:53.383 --> 00:00:55.232
The better means used for improvement.

18
00:00:55.817 --> 00:00:57.166
The better I feel.

19
00:00:57.750 --> 00:01:00.100
Your turn. Say: The better.

20
00:01:02.967 --> 00:01:03.933
The better.

21
00:01:04.683 --> 00:01:05.417
Much.

22
00:01:06.417 --> 00:01:08.347
Much means by a large amount.

23
00:01:08.950 --> 00:01:09.939
Much better.

24
00:01:10.550 --> 00:01:13.307
Your turn. Say: Much.

25
00:01:16.167 --> 00:01:17.005
Much.

26
00:01:17.750 --> 00:01:18.438
Far.

27
00:01:19.450 --> 00:01:21.357
Far means by a large amount.

28
00:01:21.950 --> 00:01:23.299
Far more difficult.

29
00:01:23.883 --> 00:01:26.211
Your turn. Say: Far.

30
00:01:29.067 --> 00:01:29.812
Far.

31
00:01:30.550 --> 00:01:31.493
Slightly.

32
00:01:32.483 --> 00:01:34.506
Slightly means by a small amount.

33
00:01:35.117 --> 00:01:36.408
Slightly colder.

34
00:01:37.017 --> 00:01:39.692
Your turn. Say: Slightly.

35
00:01:42.533 --> 00:01:43.546
Slightly.

36
00:01:44.283 --> 00:01:45.273
Twice as.

37
00:01:46.283 --> 00:01:48.550
Twice as means two times the amount.

38
00:01:49.150 --> 00:01:50.488
Twice as fast.

39
00:01:51.083 --> 00:01:53.550
Your turn. Say: Twice as.

40
00:01:56.400 --> 00:01:57.529
Twice as.

41
00:01:58.283 --> 00:01:59.308
Gradually.

42
00:02:00.317 --> 00:02:02.374
Gradually means step by step.

43
00:02:02.983 --> 00:02:04.449
Gradually improving.

44
00:02:05.050 --> 00:02:07.702
Your turn. Say: Gradually.

45
00:02:10.567 --> 00:02:11.707
Gradually.

46
00:02:12.500 --> 00:02:16.209
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:17.050 --> 00:02:19.781
Visal, complete this: the more I study, the…

48
00:02:20.883 --> 00:02:30.795
The more I study, the better I understand. This pattern shows two things changing together. Both parts begin with the and a comparative.

49
00:02:31.883 --> 00:02:33.128
How do we form it?

50
00:02:34.217 --> 00:02:46.487
The + comparative, the + comparative. The harder you work, the more you learn. The less you worry, the happier you are. Use more for long adjectives and -er for short ones.

51
00:02:47.583 --> 00:02:49.676
How do we modify comparatives?

52
00:02:50.783 --> 00:03:03.530
Much, far and a lot show a big difference: far more difficult. Slightly and a bit show a small difference. Twice as fast means two times as fast. Progress happens gradually.

53
00:03:04.667 --> 00:03:06.132
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:06.983 --> 00:03:10.376
Grammar focus: The plus comparative, the plus comparative.

55
00:03:10.676 --> 00:03:11.840
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:12.550 --> 00:03:14.700
The more I study, the better I understand.

57
00:03:15.617 --> 00:03:17.686
The harder you work, the more you learn.

58
00:03:18.583 --> 00:03:20.676
The less you worry, the happier you are.

59
00:03:21.633 --> 00:03:27.757
The + comparative, the + comparative. Use much / far for big differences and slightly for small ones.

60
00:03:28.517 --> 00:03:32.121
Be careful! Don't say: More you study, better you do.

61
00:03:34.067 --> 00:03:36.484
Say: The more you study, the better you do.

62
00:03:36.784 --> 00:03:38.853
Use the + comparative twice.

63
00:03:39.667 --> 00:03:42.435
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:43.233 --> 00:03:44.397
Growing Together.

65
00:03:44.697 --> 00:03:46.998
The more I study, the better I understand.

66
00:03:48.000 --> 00:03:50.197
The harder you work, the more you learn.

67
00:03:51.200 --> 00:03:53.118
The less you worry, the happier you are.

68
00:03:54.133 --> 00:03:57.410
Learning English is far easier when you practise every day.

69
00:03:58.400 --> 00:04:00.040
I am gradually improving.

70
00:04:01.133 --> 00:04:05.135
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:05.983 --> 00:04:08.029
The more you practise, blank you become.

72
00:04:08.329 --> 00:04:11.774
A, the better. B, better. C, the more good.

73
00:04:15.333 --> 00:04:17.670
The answer is A: the better.

74
00:04:18.817 --> 00:04:21.188
The blank you worry, the happier you are.

75
00:04:21.488 --> 00:04:24.375
A, more. B, less. C, most.

76
00:04:27.933 --> 00:04:30.061
The answer is B: less.

77
00:04:31.217 --> 00:04:34.867
This exercise is blank more difficult than that one. (much)

78
00:04:35.167 --> 00:04:38.647
A, far. B, slightly. C, twice.

79
00:04:42.200 --> 00:04:44.002
The answer is A: far.

80
00:04:45.150 --> 00:04:46.290
Which is correct?

81
00:04:46.590 --> 00:04:52.810
A, The more harder you try, the better.. B, The harder you try, the better.. C, The harder you try, better..

82
00:04:56.367 --> 00:04:59.028
The answer is B: The harder you try, the better..

83
00:05:00.183 --> 00:05:02.717
According to the reading, how is the writer improving?

84
00:05:03.017 --> 00:05:06.577
A, gradually. B, suddenly. C, never.

85
00:05:10.133 --> 00:05:12.342
The answer is A: gradually.

86
00:05:13.533 --> 00:05:17.033
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:17.883 --> 00:05:20.765
Complete this sentence: The more I study, the…

88
00:05:29.550 --> 00:05:31.004
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:31.304 --> 00:05:42.248
The more I study, the more confident I feel. The more I speak English, the less nervous I am. I improve gradually, and the results are clear.

90
00:05:42.548 --> 00:05:44.362
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:05:45.250 --> 00:05:50.422
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and the plus comparative, the plus comparative.

92
00:05:50.722 --> 00:05:56.001
Today's value is growth mindset. Mistakes help you grow. Keep learning, step by step.

93
00:05:56.301 --> 00:05:59.185
See you in Unit thirty-eight. Goodbye!

94
00:05:59.485 --> 00:06:03.020
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

